              "id": "1",
              "name": "role",
              "value": "devops-engineer",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "name": "prompt",
              "value": "=Deploy release {{ $env.RELEASE_VERSION }} to production — no rebuild, the full-version image was already retagged and pushed during promotion, and already redeployed to UAT for staging checks. For every service under env/uat/*, read its current image tag from env/uat/{service}/values.yaml, and write that same tag into env/production/{service}/values.yaml on main (create the file if this is the service's first production deploy — copy the shape of an existing env/production/*/values.yaml, or env/uat/*/values.yaml if none exists yet). Commit all edited files in one commit ('chore: deploy {{ $env.RELEASE_VERSION }} to production') and push to main — ArgoCD's automated syncPolicy on each production Application picks it up from there (no image-updater on production, explicit sync only, same as UAT). Then wait for each service's production Deployment rollout to complete (kubectl --context $PRODUCTION_CLUSTER_CONTEXT rollout status deployment/<service> -n hr-portal --timeout=120s) before reporting done — do not report success until rollout is actually confirmed, not just committed.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "name": "story",
              "value": "={{ $env.RELEASE_VERSION }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
